<% content_for :title, "Income Tax Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Income Tax calculator page (spec issue #260, DESIGN.md BLEND) — iteration-0007's one new
  primitive: PROGRESSIVE BRACKET math. Apply the pinned 2025 US federal single-filer
  ordinary-income brackets to a taxable income and show the total tax (the hero), the
  effective + marginal rates (stat grid), and the per-bracket breakdown (the tabular-output
  data table).

  Two ways to enter income — the spec's either/or resolution (taxable_income entered
  directly, OR gross_income − deductions). The frontend turns that into a MODE PICKER: a
  native radio <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode], showing only the active mode's
  field(s). The backend ignores `mode` (not a declared attribute) and resolves from whichever
  income source it receives — so the controller DISABLES the inactive mode's inputs, sending
  exactly one income source. The form posts over Turbo and re-renders #result in place; it
  works WITHOUT JS — both field blocks are present, the server resolves the income from
  whatever is filled, and re-renders the result fragment.

  Mode-picker choice (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): TWO modes (N=2) but both labels read as
  multi-word ("Taxable income" / "Gross income & deductions"). The §4 rule reserves the
  segmented control for N ≤ 3 with SHORT labels; a multi-word label routes to the SELECTABLE
  OPTION LIST (.mode-option), with a helper line per row.

  Layout per DESIGN.md §3 — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), collapsing to one
  column on mobile. Spacing scale ("targets not minimums"):
    • stacked fields → space-y-5
    • major blocks within the card (mode → fields → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier)
    • column gutters / card padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier)
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Financial</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Income Tax Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Your <span class="font-semibold text-ink">2025 US federal income tax</span> on your
    taxable income, using the progressive single-filer brackets — with the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">per-bracket breakdown</span> and your effective and
    marginal rates. Enter your taxable income directly, or your gross income and deductions.
    Every figure is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/income_tax", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "income-tax" } do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — selectable option list (.mode-option), per DESIGN.md §4: two multi-word
          modes → one bordered, divided container of full-width rows, NOT a segmented control
          (reserved for N ≤ 3 short labels). The accessible control is a native radio
          <fieldset>/<legend> posting inputs[mode]; each radio is visually-hidden (peer sr-only)
          and paired to a styled <label for>. The active row is painted with no JS via
          peer:checked, and the .mode-option::before radio glyph is the non-colour active cue
          (DESIGN.md §6). Each row names HOW income is entered (bold label) + a helper. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="text-xs font-bold text-label">How do you want to enter income?</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% income_tax_modes.each_with_index do |m, i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, m[:value],
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { income_tax_target: "modeInput", action: "income-tax#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: m[:value],
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { income_tax_target: "modeOption", mode: m[:value] } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= m[:label] %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= m[:helper] %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Fields. Stacked tier: space-y-5 down the column (DESIGN.md §3). Each field block
          declares the single mode it serves via data-income-tax-mode; Stimulus shows only the
          active mode's block(s) and disables the others' inputs so only one income source is
          posted (the no-JS baseline shows all — the server resolves whatever is filled). Every
          money input carries a leading $ affix on the Affix tier (gap-2). %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# Taxable income — the `taxable` mode only. The directly-entered figure the brackets
            apply to. %>
        <div data-income-tax-target="field" data-income-tax-mode="taxable">
          <%= f.label :taxable_income, "Taxable income", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_taxable_income" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :taxable_income, id: "inputs_taxable_income", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Gross income — the `gross` mode only. Total income before deductions. %>
        <div data-income-tax-target="field" data-income-tax-mode="gross">
          <%= f.label :gross_income, "Gross income", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_gross_income" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :gross_income, id: "inputs_gross_income", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Deductions — the `gross` mode only. Subtracted from gross to find taxable income
            (floored at 0). Optional; defaults to 0 server-side. %>
        <div data-income-tax-target="field" data-income-tax-mode="gross">
          <%= f.label :deductions, "Deductions", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_deductions" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">$</span>
            <%= f.number_field :deductions, id: "inputs_deductions", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  min: "0", placeholder: "0.00", class: "field-input" %>
          </div>
          <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs text-muted">Standard or itemized — leave blank for none.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate tax",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target) ─────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
